H800.definition:
feminine of H784 (אֵשׁ);
fire
KJV: fire.

H801.definition:
the same as H800 (אֶשָּׁה), but used in a liturgical sense;
properly, a burnt-offering; but occasionally of any sacrifice
KJV: (offering, sacrifice), (made) by fire.

H803.definition:
feminine passive participle from an unused root meaning to found;
foundation
KJV: foundation.

H804.definition:
or אַשֻּׁר; apparently from H833 (אָשַׁר) (in the sense of successful);
Ashshur, the second son of Shem; also his descendants and the country occupied by them (i.e. Assyria), its region and its empire
KJV: Asshur, Assur, Assyria, Assyrians. See H838 (אָשֻׁר).

H805.definition:
or אַשּׁוּרִי; from a patrial word of the same form as H804 (אַשּׁוּר);
an Ashurite (collectively) or inhabitant of Ashur, a district in Palestine
KJV: Asshurim, Ashurites.

H806.definition:
probably from H7835 (שָׁחַר); black;
Ashchur, an Israelite
KJV: Ashur.

H807.definition:
of foreign origin;
Ashima, a deity of Hamath
KJV: Ashima.

H808.definition:
from the same as H784 (אֵשׁ) (in the sense of pressing down firmly; compare H803 (אֲשׁוּיָה));
a (ruined) foundation
KJV: foundation.

H809.definition:
feminine of H808 (אָשִׁישׁ);
something closely pressed together, i.e. a cake of raisins or other comfits
KJV: flagon.

H810.definition:
from an unused root (probably meaning to bunch together);
a testicle (as a lump)
KJV: stone.

H811.definition:
or אֶשְׁכֹּל; probably prolonged from H810 (אֶשֶׁךְ);
a bunch of grapes or other fruit
KJV: cluster (of grapes).

H812.definition:
the same as H811 (אֶשְׁכּוֹל);
Eshcol, the name of an Amorite, also of a valley in Palestine
KJV: Eshcol.

H813.definition:
of foreign origin;
Ashkenaz, a Japhethite, also his descendants
KJV: Ashkenaz.

H814.definition:
for H7939 (שָׂכָר);
a gratuity
KJV: gift, present.

H815.definition:
from a root of uncertain signification;
a tamarisk tree; by extension, a grove of any kind
KJV: grove, tree.

H816.definition:
or אָשֵׁם; a primitive root;
to be guilty; by implication to be punished or perish
KJV: [idiom] certainly, be(-come, made) desolate, destroy, [idiom] greatly, be(-come, found, hold) guilty, offend (acknowledge offence), trespass.

H817.definition:
from H816 (אָשַׁם);
guilt; by implication, a fault; also a sin-offering
KJV: guiltiness, (offering for) sin, trespass (offering).

H818.definition:
from H816 (אָשַׁם);
guilty; hence, presenting asin-offering
KJV: one which is faulty, guilty.

H819.definition:
feminine of H817 (אָשָׁם);
guiltiness, a fault, the presentation of asin-offering
KJV: offend, sin, (cause of) trespass(-ing, offering).

H820.definition:
probably from H8081 (שֶׁמֶן);
a fat-field
KJV: desolate place.

H821.definition:
or אַשׁמוּרָה; or אַשׁמֹרֶת; (feminine) from H8104 (שָׁמַר);
a night watch
KJV: watch.

H822.definition:
apparently from an unused root (probably meaning to leave interstices);
a latticed window
KJV: casement, lattice.

H823.definition:
probably a variation for H3466 (יְשָׁנָה);
Ashnah, the name of two places in Palestine
KJV: Ashnah.

H824.definition:
from H8172 (שָׁעַן); support;
Eshan, a place in Palestine
KJV: Eshean.

H825.definition:
from an unused root (probably meaning to lisp, i.e. practice enchantment);
a conjurer
KJV: astrologer.

H826.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H825 (אַשָּׁף)
{a conjurer}
KJV: astrologer.

H827.definition:
perhaps (feminine) from the same as H825 (אַשָּׁף) (in the sense of covering);
a quiver or arrow-case
KJV: quiver.

H828.definition:
of foreign origin;
Ashpenaz, a Babylonian eunuch
KJV: Ashpenaz.

H829.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
a measured portion
KJV: good piece (of flesh).

H830.definition:
or אַשְׁפּוֹת; or שְׁפֹת; (contraction) plural of a noun of the same form as H827 (אַשְׁפָּה), from H8192 (שָׁפָה) (in the sense of scraping);
a heap of rubbish or filth
KJV: dung (hill).

H831.definition:
probably from H8254 (שָׁקַל) in the sense of weighing-place (i.e. mart);
Ashkelon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Ashkelon, Askalon.

H832.definition:
patrial from H831 (אַשְׁקְלוֹן);
Ashkelonite (collectively) or inhabitant of Ashkelon
KJV: Eshkalonites.

H833.definition:
or אָשֵׁר; a primitive root;
to be straight (used in the widest sense, especially to be level, right, happy); figuratively, to go forward, be honest, proper
KJV: (call, be) bless(-ed, happy), go, guide, lead, relieve.

H834.definition:
a primitive relative pronoun (of every gender and number);
who, which, what, that; also (as an adverb and a conjunction) when, where, how, because, in order that, etc.
KJV: [idiom] after, [idiom] alike, as (soon as), because, [idiom] every, for, [phrase] forasmuch, [phrase] from whence, [phrase] how(-soever), [idiom] if, (so) that ((thing) which, wherein), [idiom] though, [phrase] until, [phrase] whatsoever, when, where ([phrase] -as, -in, -of, -on, -soever, -with), which, whilst, [phrase] whither(-soever), who(-m, -soever, -se). As it is indeclinable, it is often accompanied by the personal pronoun expletively, used to show the connection.

H835.definition:
from H833 (אָשַׁר);
happiness; only in masculine plural construction as interjection, how happy!
KJV: blessed, happy.

H836.definition:
from H833 (אָשַׁר),
happy; Asher, a son of Jacob, and the tribe descended from him, with its territory; also a place in Palestine
KJV: Asher

H838.definition:
or אַשֻּׁר; from H833 (אָשַׁר) in the sense of going;
a step
KJV: going, step.

H839.definition:
contracted for H8391 (תְּאַשּׁוּר);
the cedar tree or some other light elastic wood
KJV: Ashurite.

H840.definition:
by orthographical variation from H833 (אָשַׁר) and H410 (אֵל); right of God;
Asarel, an Israelite
KJV: Asareel.

H841.definition:
from the same as H840 (אֲשַׂרְאֵל); right toward God;
Asarelah, an Israelite
KJV: Asarelah. Compare H3480 (יְשַׂרְאֵלָה).

H842.definition:
or אֲשֵׁירָה; from H833 (אָשַׁר); happy;
Asherah (or Astarte) a Phoenician goddess; also an image of the same
KJV: grove. Compare H6253 (עַשְׁתֹּרֶת).

H843.definition:
patronymic from H836 (אָשֵׁר);
an Asherite (collectively) or descendant of Asher
KJV: Asherites.

H844.definition:
an orthographical variation for H840 (אֲשַׂרְאֵל);
Asriel, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Ashriel, Asriel.

H845.definition:
patronymic from H844 (אַשְׂרִיאֵל);
an Asrielite (collectively) or descendant of Asriel
KJV: Asrielites.

H846.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H833 (אָשַׁר);
a wall (from its uprightness)
KJV: wall.

H847.definition:
or אֶשְׁתָּאוֹל; probably from H7592 (שָׁאַל); intreaty;
Eshtaol, a place in Palestine
KJV: Eshtaol.

H848.definition:
patrial from H847 (אֶשְׁתָּאֹל);
an Eshtaolite (collectively) or inhabitant of Eshtaol
KJV: Eshtaulites.

H849.definition:
(Aramaic) from H7712 (שְׁדַר) (in a bad sense);
rebellion
KJV: sedition.

H850.definition:
probably from the same as H7764 (שׁוּנִי); restful;
Eshton, an Israelite
KJV: Eshton.

H851.definition:
or אֶשְׁתְּמוֹעַ; or אֶשְׁתְּמֹה; from H8085 (שָׁמַע) (in the sense of obedience);
Eshtemoa or Eshtemoh, a place in Palestine
KJV: Eshtemoa, Eshtemoh.

H852.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H226 (אוֹת);
a portent
KJV: sign.

H853.definition:
apparent contracted from H226 (אוֹת) in the demonstrative sense of entity;
properly, self (but generally used to point out more definitely the object of a verb or preposition, even or namely)
KJV: (as such unrepresented in English).

H854.definition:
probably from H579 (אָנָה);
properly, nearness (used only as a preposition or an adverb), near; hence, generally, with, by, at, among, etc.
KJV: against, among, before, by, for, from, in(-to), (out) of, with. Often with another prepositional prefix.

H855.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
a hoe or other digging implement
KJV: coulter, plowshare.

H856.definition:
from H854 (אֵת) and H1168 (בַּעַל); with Baal;
Ethbaal, a Phoenician king
KJV: Ethbaal.

H857.definition:
or אָתָא; a primitive root (collateral to H225 (אוּת) contraction);
to arrive
KJV: (be-, things to) come (upon), bring.

H858.definition:
(Aramaic) or אָתָא; (Aramaic), corresponding to H857 (אָתָה)
{to arrive}
KJV: (be-) come, bring.

H859.definition:
or (shortened); אַתָּ; or אַת; feminine (irregular) sometimes אַתִּי; plural masculine אַתֶּם; feminine אַתֶּן; or אַתֵּנָהlemma אתֵּנָה missing vowel, corrected to אַתֵּנָה; or אַתֵּנָּה; a primitive pronoun of the second person;
thou and thee, or (plural) ye and you
KJV: thee, thou, ye, you.

H860.definition:
probably from the same as H386 (אֵיתָן) (in the sense of patience);
a female donkey (from its docility)
KJV: (she) ass.

H861.definition:
(Aramaic) probably from the corresponding to H784 (אֵשׁ);
probably a fire-place, i.e. furnace
KJV: furnace.

H862.definition:
or אַתִּיק; from H5423 (נָתַק) in the sense of decreasing;
a ledge or offset in abuilding
KJV: gallery.

H863.definition:
or אִיתַי; from H854 (אֵת); near;
Ittai or Ithai, the name of a Gittite and of an Israelite
KJV: Ithai, Ittai.

H864.definition:
of Egyptian derivation;
Etham, a place in the Desert
KJV: Etham.

H865.definition:
or אִתְמוֹל; or אֶתְמוּל; probably from H853 (אֵת) or H854 (אֵת) and H4136 (מוּל);
heretofore; definitely yesterday
KJV: [phrase] before (that) time, [phrase] heretofore, of late (old), [phrase] times past, yester(day).

H866.definition:
from H8566 (תָּנָה);
a present (as the price of harlotry)
KJV: reward.

H867.definition:
perhaps from H866 (אֶתְנָה); munificence;
Ethni, an Israelite
KJV: Ethni.

H868.definition:
the same as H866 (אֶתְנָה);
a gift (as the price of harlotry or idolatry)
KJV: hire, reward.

H869.definition:
the same as H868 (אֶתְנַן) in the sense of H867 (אֶתְנִי);
Ethnan, an Israelite
KJV: Ethnan.

H870.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to that of H871 (אֲתָרִים);
a place; (adverb) after
KJV: after, place.

H871.definition:
plural from an unused root (probably meaning to step); places;
Atharim, a place near Palestine
KJV: spies. b

H872.definition:
from H935 (בּוֹא);
an entrance to a building
KJV: entry.

H874.definition:
a primitive root;
to dig; by analogy, to engrave; figuratively, to explain
KJV: declare, (make) plain(-ly).

H875.definition:
from H874 (בָּאַר);
a pit; especially a well
KJV: pit, well.

H876.definition:
the same as H875 (בְּאֵר);
Beer, a place in the Desert, also one in Palestine
KJV: Beer.

H877.definition:
from H874 (בָּאַר);
a cistern
KJV: cistern.

H878.definition:
from H875 (בְּאֵר); a well;
Beera, an Israelite
KJV: Beera.

H879.definition:
from H875 (בְּאֵר) and the plural of H410 (אֵל); well of heroes;
Beer-Elim, a place in the Desert
KJV: Beer-elim.

H880.definition:
the same as H878 (בְּאֵרָא);
Beerah, an Israelite
KJV: Beerah.

H881.definition:
feminine plural of H875 (בְּאֵר); wells;
Beeroth, a place in Palestine
KJV: Beeroth.

H882.definition:
from H875 (בְּאֵר); fountained;
Beeri, the name of a Hittite and of an Israelite
KJV: Beeri.

H883.definition:
from H875 (בְּאֵר) and H2416 (חַי) (with prefix) and H7203 (רֹאֶה); well of a living (One) my Seer;
Beer-Lachai-Roi, a place in the Desert
KJV: Beer-lahai-roi.

H884.definition:
from H875 (בְּאֵר) and H7651 (שֶׁבַע) (in the sense of H7650 (שָׁבַע)); well of an oath;
Beer-Sheba, a place in Palestine
KJV: Beer-shebah.

H885.definition:
from the feminine plural of H875 (בְּאֵר), and the plural contraction of H1121 (בֵּן), and H3292 (יַעֲקָן); wells of (the) sons of Jaakan;
Beeroth-Bene-Jaakan, a place in the Desert
KJV: Beeroth of the children of Jaakan.

H886.definition:
patrial from H881 (בְּאֵרוֹת);
a Beerothite or inhabitant of Beeroth
KJV: Beerothite.

H887.definition:
a primitive root;
to smell bad; figuratively, to be offensive morally
KJV: (make to) be abhorred (had in abomination, loathsome, odious), (cause a, make to) stink(-ing savour), [idiom] utterly.

H888.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H887 (בָּאַשׁ)
{to smell bad; figuratively, to be offensive morally}
KJV: displease.

H889.definition:
from H877 (בֹּאר);
a stench
KJV: stink.

H890.definition:
feminine of H889 (בְּאֹשׁ);
stink-weed or any other noxious or useless plant
KJV: cockle.

H891.definition:
plural of H889 (בְּאֹשׁ);
poison-berries
KJV: wild grapes.

H892.definition:
feminine active participle of an unused root meaning to hollow out;
something hollowed (as a gate), i.e. pupil of the eye
KJV: apple (of the eye).

H893.definition:
probably of foreign origin;
Bebai, an Israelite
KJV: Bebai.

H894.definition:
from H1101 (בָּלַל); confusion;
Babel (i.e. Babylon), including Babylonia and the Babylonian empire
KJV: Babel, Babylon.

H895.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H894 (בָּבֶל)
{Babel (i.e. Babylon), including Babylonia and the Babylonian empire}
KJV: Babylon.

H896.definition:
(Aramaic) patrial from H895 (בַּבֶל);
a Babylonian
KJV: Babylonia.

H897.definition:
a Persian word;
food
KJV: spoil (from the margin for H957 (בַּז).)

H898.definition:
a primitive root;
to cover (with a garment); figuratively, to act covertly; by implication, to pillage
KJV: deal deceitfully (treacherously, unfaithfully), offend, transgress(-or), (depart), treacherous (dealer, -ly, man), unfaithful(-ly, man), [idiom] very.

H899.definition:
from H898 (בָּגַד);
a covering, i.e. clothing; also treachery or pillage
KJV: apparel, cloth(-es, ing), garment, lap, rag, raiment, robe, [idiom] very (treacherously), vesture, wardrobe.
